    3. Per legend, design unit_sprite (NxN, 2 colors, fully filled), frame mask (H x W, single color, 8-connected, active cells = 50-65% of H*W), anchor (pr,pc) in {0,1,2}^2, rotation k in {0,1,2,3}.
    4. Compute rotated composite size; ensure it fits within canvas_h x canvas_w at chosen anchor. For 2 legends, ensure composites don't overlap. Reject/resample if not.
    5. Build canvas background with 2 colors in horizontal or vertical bands (band width >= 4).
    6. Build output by overlaying each rotated composite at its anchor position.
    7. Build input by placing unmodified canvas (no overlay) into the grid, adding legend columns with unit sprite (color-swapped back), frame, marker square, and rotation patch, separated by all-6 columns.
    8. Validate via solver.

